//! The built-in sample text.

/// Short, repetitive sentences about a garden: easy patterns for a first run to
/// pick up, long enough for the largest starting point and a held-back check.
pub(super) const SAMPLE_TEXT: &str = concat!(
    "The sun warms the garden. The rain waters the garden. We plant seeds in the garden. The seeds grow into flowers. The flowers bring bees. We care for the garden together. ",
    "In spring the garden wakes. The soil is soft and dark. We dig small rows with a spade. We drop the seeds into the rows. We cover the seeds with soil. The rain falls on the rows, and the seeds begin to grow. ",
    "In summer the garden is tall and green. The beans climb the poles. The peas hang in their pods. The tomatoes turn from green to red. The bees move from flower to flower. We water the garden in the cool of the evening. ",
    "In autumn the garden gives back. We pick the apples from the tree. We pull the carrots from the soil. We carry the pumpkins to the kitchen. We save some seeds in a paper bag. The leaves fall and cover the beds. ",
    "In winter the garden rests. The beds sleep under the leaves. The birds come for the last berries. We clean the spade and the rake. We read about new flowers by the fire. We plan the rows for the spring. ",
    "Every morning we walk to the garden gate. We look at the beans and the peas. We look at the flowers and the bees. We pull a few weeds from the rows. We fill the can and water the pots. Then we sit on the bench and listen to the birds. ",
    "The garden teaches us to wait. A seed does not hurry. A flower opens when it is ready. The rain comes when it comes. We do a little each day, and the garden does the rest. ",
    "The children like the garden best. They count the bees on the flowers. They look for worms in the soil. They eat the peas straight from the pod. They water the pots, and they water their shoes. They ask when the pumpkins will be ready. ",
    "Our neighbours share the garden with us. One brings seeds for red flowers. One brings a cutting from an old rose. One shows us how to tie the beans to the poles. We give them tomatoes in the summer and apples in the autumn. A garden grows better when we care for it together. ",
    "When the sun goes down, the garden is quiet. The bees go home. The flowers close. The soil holds the warmth of the day. We hang the spade on its hook and close the gate. Tomorrow the sun will warm the garden again. ",
);
